From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] keyhandler: match Alt+Shift letters by their lowercase name

Every Alt+Shift global key was dead: Alt+Shift+F (Frame), Alt+Shift+M
(Settings), Alt+Shift+O (search), Alt+Shift+Q (logout) and Alt+Shift+D
(dump UI tree) all did nothing.

Holding Shift makes the keyval the capital letter, so
Gdk.keyval_name() returns 'M', not 'm'. The branch that builds the
'<alt><shift>' prefix tested membership in ['f', 'm', 'o', 'q', 'd'], so
it never fired, the key stayed 'M', and _actions_table - which is keyed
'<alt><shift>m' - never matched. The shell log shows it plainly:

  WARNING:root:GTK4 semantic key event: Alt_L
  WARNING:root:GTK4 semantic key event: Shift_L
  WARNING:root:GTK4 semantic key event: M

and no control panel.

Test the lowercase form and build the key from it.

--- a/src/jarabe/view/keyhandler.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/view/keyhandler.py
@@ -276,9 +276,12 @@
                 key = '<alt>Escape'
             elif key in ['F11', 'F12']:
                 key = '<alt>' + key
-            elif key in ['f', 'm', 'o', 'q', 'd']:
+            elif key.lower() in ['f', 'm', 'o', 'q', 'd']:
                 if state & Gdk.ModifierType.SHIFT_MASK:
-                    key = '<alt><shift>' + key
+                    # Shift makes the keyval - and so keyval_name() - the
+                    # capital letter, but _actions_table is keyed by the
+                    # lowercase one.
+                    key = '<alt><shift>' + key.lower()
 
         if key in _actions_table:
             action = _actions_table[key]
